WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Hi my name is Luca, from LucaLampariello.com, and today we're going to talk about love.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.020
A few weeks ago I was sitting at a
table at a tandem event, and all of a

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.550
sudden, someone asked me a very peculiar
question - we were talking about language

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:24.240
learning and it turned out that I speak
a few languages myself, and I had some

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.900
foreign partners, and this girl asked me:
"do you pick up girls to learn languages

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.190
or do you learn languages to pick up
girls?" And I admit that the question

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:40.320
kind of caught me off guard and got me
thinking at the same time, so I've been

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.629
thinking about my experiences and the
lessons I've learned and here it is,

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:48.400
I wanted to share them with you today

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.620
The very first important lesson that
I've learned when it comes to speaking

00:00:55.620 --> 00:01:01.109
foreign languages with your foreign
partner is that you should at least

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:06.570
speak their language at an intermediate
level. I still remember that when I met

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:11.400
my ex French girlfriend I spoke French
relatively well and the same happened

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.700
with my ex Russian girlfriend and I am
sure that if I hadn't spoken those

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.630
languages at a good level I would have
never spoken or practiced these

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.250
languages because we would have reversed, 
we would have resorted to - go figure -

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:32.340
English! And I've learned that once you
start a relationship in a specific

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.409
language, that relationship solidifies
and coalesces around the language, and it is

00:01:37.409 --> 00:01:42.479
really difficult to change languages,
switch languages down the line, so the

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:47.100
first lesson I've learned is learn
languages because the more languages you

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.909
learn, the more opportunities you
have. You never know, maybe today you're

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:54.689
going to stumble upon a girl or a guy
who speaks the language you're learning

00:01:54.689 --> 00:02:02.300
and remember: every language you learn
makes you closer to millions of people potentially.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:10.190
The second important lesson I've learned
is that language learning doesn't happen

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:15.380
automatically in general, and doesn't
happen automatically even if you have a

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:19.580
partner. You still have to put in the
effort. So you might be thinking that

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.700
since you have a partner, you might want
to get every chance you get to practice

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:33.020
that language with her or with him, but
your partner is your love partner, you

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:38.660
share love with them, not ...you know.. he or  she is not your language

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:44.959
partner, so you have to make a compromise,
you have to learn but you don't have to

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:50.030
pester them with too many questions
because otherwise they're going to get -

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:56.000
they're gonna get the idea that you are
there to use them. How to do that? My

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.980
advice is to keep learning on your own,
get massive input, get into the habit of

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.840
listening, reading, and then also on top
of that, if you have the chance of

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.769
practicing languages for
example on the internet, or with other

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:14.360
friends that's great! Then
the cherry on the cake is to practice

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:22.000
with your partner, but that's the cherry on the cake, you should do bulk of the work yourself.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.299
The third
lesson I've learned is that when it

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:34.459
comes to having a foreign partner, you
get your fair share of embarrassing

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:39.560
moments, of misunderstandings of misusing
words, or saying one word thinking that

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:43.610
you're saying something while you're
saying something else. Meet the parents

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:49.010
meet the circle of friends. This is all
part of the beautiful adventure of

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.950
having a foreign girlfriend or a foreign
boyfriend so I've had my fair share of

00:03:54.950 --> 00:04:00.540
embarrassing moments but I accept them
and I know that this is all part of this

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:08.500
beautiful trip that is language learning and getting to know foreign cultures and foreign people.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.390
So here you have it, I hope that it was useful

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:16.750
if you have a tandem, a foreign boyfriend
or girlfriend, please share your stories

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:21.310
your everything - ranging from
embarrassing situations to

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:25.930
lovely moments with your partner, 
families and friends. You can click

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:30.190
in the description box to check on the
link to an article that I have written

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:34.150
about this, where I share my very
personal stories and in particular my

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:38.920
first kiss in Ireland and how language
learning played a huge role. Especially

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.600
speaking English with an American accent
made all the difference.

